# Use the image CMD instead of replacing it with `sleep infinity`.
#
# The Dockerfile CMD boots cupsd with the vulnerable TLS config and then execs
# `sleep infinity`, so:
#   * the daemon is ALREADY RUNNING (accepting deprecated TLSv1.0/1.1) when the
#     agent starts, which is what makes the "fixed the config but never
#     restarted the service" case detectable;
#   * PID 1 is still `sleep infinity`, so restarting cupsd cannot kill the
#     container.
#
# Consequence for solutions: a fix must (re)start the remediation and leave the
# live TLS surface hardened - merely editing config is not enough.
